{"sequence":16,"timestamp":"2026-03-29T21:39:35.971884902Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-1-d5896362","body":"In conservation_regression.rs, the grazing test (closed_system_grazing_conserves_n_and_c, lines 257-271) still uses bare `assert!()` for pathway verification instead of the new `assert_or_dump()` helper that all other five tests use. This means a grazing pathway assertion failure will NOT dump the trace to /tmp/tank_conservation_traces/grazing.jsonl, violating the acceptance criterion that 'failures dump the full trace to a file for debugging.' Replace the three bare `assert!()` calls with `assert_or_dump(\"grazing\", &engine, ...)` calls.","dedup_key":"f0f67ad8cb8b07078db7a771b949422f4b66302748bcbc16a570dcaf927f4195","run_id":"run-20260329204233","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":17,"timestamp":"2026-03-29T21:39:35.981562309Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-1-0ed6fb15","body":"In e2e_conservation.rs, `run_grazing()` (lines 375-390) has no pathway-verification assertions (ensure/ensure_trace_delta), while all other five scenario runners (run_feeding, run_mortality_senescence, run_trim_and_remove, run_trim_and_leave, run_water_change) were enhanced with these checks in this diff. Add at minimum: ensure that periphyton decreased, TAN increased, and fine detritus increased (mirroring the unit test), so the e2e runner catches the case where grazing is silently not exercised.","dedup_key":"7b62325a4c301d88ca782d0d22b6ad0f24c40d902de1aee4ee1a772eb59c8f36","run_id":"run-20260329204233","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":18,"timestamp":"2026-03-29T21:39:35.991342139Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-1-bd5aaa0c","body":"In the water-change test (both files), the expected_n_import calculation only sums `source.ammonia_mg_n_per_l + source.nitrate_mg_n_per_l + source.don_mg_n_per_l`, omitting `source.nitrite_mg_n_per_l`. The engine's budget (apply_water_change_with_budget, line 125-128) sums all four source species including nitrite. This only works because the source profile's nitrite is implicitly zero from SourceWaterProfile::zero(). Add `+ source.nitrite_mg_n_per_l` to the test's expected_n_import formula for correctness and resilience against fixture evolution.","dedup_key":"50c59db72fd752e94caf60972a951aa153c222c5b113e2970f6fa52bc0b4b9a6","run_id":"run-20260329204233","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
