{"sequence":45,"timestamp":"2026-03-29T22:42:44.032656977Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-3-e46f2f7d","body":"The 6 conservation test fixtures in `conservation_regression.rs` are copied verbatim into `e2e_conservation.rs` (grazing_fixture, feeding_fixture, mortality_senescence_fixture, trim_fixture, water_change_fixture, plus helpers close_gas_exchange, disable_dic_shortcuts, dump_trace). Extract shared fixtures into a `test_fixtures` module (e.g. `crates/tank_core/tests/common/conservation_fixtures.rs`) or a `#[cfg(test)]` module in tank_core that both test files import. This prevents silent divergence when a fixture is updated in one file but not the other.","dedup_key":"368a15222a09a48376e19b5f782cd48f783349700c435dbfd90f7de87120721b","run_id":"run-20260329204233","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":46,"timestamp":"2026-03-29T22:42:44.040998116Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-3-f6f2eb7f","body":"Test 3 (`closed_system_mortality_senescence_conserves_n_and_c`) verifies trace evidence for plant senescence → detritus and algae senescence → detritus, but does not verify shrimp death → detritus via an explicit `assert_trace_delta` for `system:daily_shrimp` / `detritus.fine_g`. Add a trace assertion that shrimp death routes biomass to fine detritus, matching the doc comment's claim that 'shrimp death and plant senescence route biomass to detritus.'","dedup_key":"46636d2937b6a1a0a78cfc95c474b4e0976f7fcdd4a4a6ef9031a6bcf8abccd1","run_id":"run-20260329204233","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
